WEBVTT

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:14.620
TJ and Gil show up at
the pre-race party for racers.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:17.200
Shut up! Stop causing a scene!

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.950
Shadows move behind the curtains of the race.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.950
Be careful, Appare--you might die.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:56.870
The first day of the race!

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:59.660
"Episode 6: I am Gil!"
Here in the pre-race goal of Lancaster,

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:00.790
"Episode 6: I am Gil!"
spectators eagerly wait for
the racers to arrive!

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:04.040
spectators eagerly wait for
the racers to arrive!

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:19.830
Tsk! Our cars are evenly matched, huh?

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.910
Move! Move! Move! Gil's coming through!

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:41.870
Where's Appare? I guess his
steam engine can't keep up.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:50.080
Appare?! He cut through the mountains?!

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:55.330
Yeah! We made it to the front!

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:58.250
Look closer. Al's further ahead.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:02.080
Ugh... So much for getting prize money.

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:06.870
Hototo! Weren't there any better shortcuts?

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:10.160
Shut up, Kosame! The race ain't over yet!

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.200
Shit!

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:01.540
We'll make it!

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:05.000
What?! Where to now?!

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.540
Hurry up!

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:16.160
We're gonna crash!

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:25.120
We'll reach the city first
and cut off the group!

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:26.700
Not happening!

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:41.200
Argh, shit! Appare!

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:07.000
First is Dylan followed by TJ!
The Thousand Three take first and second!

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:10.620
The tail of the pack comes pouring in!

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:17.120
Meh!

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.410
Dylan, congratulations!

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:22.700
How's it feel to win?

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:24.540
How will you use the ten grand?

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:25.790
Do the usual.

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:27.080
R-Right.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:28.910
The rest is all you.

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:31.000
What a spectacular race!

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:34.410
Dylan G. Oldin in a GM-made car!
It's an unbeatable combination!

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:37.160
I didn't lose because of my car.

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:42.160
Yeah, it's a nice car. Did papa buy it for you?

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:46.160
It's because I wasn't good enough.
Next time, I won't lose.

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:49.450
There is no next time.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:52.910
Not if we're fighting for our lives.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.830
If we can leave in eight hours, that's...

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:01.790
12:07 AM.

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:03.750
Ah, thanks.

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:07.200
Middle of the night, huh?

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.870
I knew this race would be tough, but damn...

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.830
I'm getting us food and water for tomorrow.

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:16.120
Great. Just a day's worth.

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:17.290
Got it.

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:19.250
Wait up, Hototo. I'll help.

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:22.370
Don't need to. I'm just getting it from there.

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:23.830
Oh...

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:27.580
It's that guy...

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:32.160
Hello! I'm sorry about earlier!

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.080
Huh?

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:36.500
An animal jumped out so I swerved.

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:40.080
I'm really sorry. I can be such a klutz.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:44.200
Oh, uh... If that's what happened,
it's no big deal.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:48.870
That's a nice car there. I'm Richard Reaseman.

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:50.790
It's a pleasure.

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:53.080
What a bright-looking kid.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:57.120
Bye! Let's have a good race!

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:03.950
I thought everyone was wild or nuts,
but there's good people, too.

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:09.580
Hey, Appare! Try to get some rest!
We've got a ways to go!

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:12.250
I don't wanna win with shortcuts.

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:13.290
Eh?

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:16.700
I want this car to put me in the lead.

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:18.450
Is that even possible?

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:20.450
Don't bug me unless there's food.

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:21.830
Yeah, yeah.

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:29.080
Give us food, water, and gasoline.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:30.950
These are supplies for racers, not--

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:35.750
We're Gil's henchmen! You got a problem?!

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:40.580
Gil's henchmen who swear
loyalty to him have that tattoo.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:44.370
The guy you're after is probably one of them.

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:47.660
Hey! What do you need?

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:50.660
Um, water and food.

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:57.790
The car's on the west side
of the pit. Go get started on it.

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.040
Yes, sir!

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.040
Al!

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:03.250
Sofia, are you okay?

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:05.830
That should be my line, right?

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:10.950
What is it?

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:12.500
Huh? What?

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:17.660
Whenever you get quiet like this,
you always have something to say.

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:22.700
Sofia, it's fine if you go ahead
and wait in New York.

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:23.540
Huh?

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:26.040
You can take the train from here.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:30.450
I know my dad asked you to be here.

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:33.750
But the race is bound to get hectic
and dangerous sooner or--

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:35.330
Am I a bother?

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:38.500
Huh? No, you aren't, but...

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:42.370
Don't even think about
risking your life over this.

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:43.830
Huh?

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:47.540
Your race isn't over till you're safe back home.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.750
You're right.

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:53.950
I'm not anything like Dylan or TJ.

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:59.250
I'm not going to put my life at risk
just to win the race.

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:02.580
I'll win, protecting the things I love.

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:05.540
That's my way of doing things.

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:09.160
I'm coming with you then.

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:14.700
I'll have the team with me,
and won't I be safe around you?

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:16.410
That's right.

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:18.830
Even you feel insecure, huh?

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:22.290
What? I-I'm not insecure!

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:27.290
Kosame!

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:30.620
Oh, Sofia! You caught up with us?

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:33.540
Yup! Are you training during the race?

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:35.410
Yeah, to kill time!

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:39.040
Leaders must be prepared at all times.

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:41.410
Perfect. Be my opponent.

00:09:41.410 --> 00:09:42.870
Huh? But...

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:46.500
I'll pay. I need to keep myself active.

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:04.500
What's wrong? Come at me!

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:17.910
I-I'm beat! That's Al for you.

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:23.330
That was good exercise.

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:27.450
Ooh! Thanks!

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:36.500
Kosame's stronger than he looks
to make you get serious like that.

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:38.580
I didn't get serious.

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:42.450
But it's true--I can't quite
gauge how strong he is.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:43.290
Huh?

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:47.540
What's more, I've never seen
such slippery swordplay.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.250
Because he used wood?

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:51.410
Not quite.

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:57.500
It's like a heavy fog is concealing his sword.

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:03.910
So it's your treat and you really don't mind?

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:08.330
Help yourself. The supply food is bland anyway.

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:10.290
Don't mind if I do.

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:18.200
That hit the spot!

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:20.200
Ain't it tasty, Hototo?

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:22.620
It's not like you cooked it.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:23.450
Food is a

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:25.620
--Gift from the Earth.
--gift from the Earth.

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:28.040
But it's also my treat.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:32.080
Appare, what's your route for tomorrow?

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:33.000
Route?

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:34.580
Through Death Valley.

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:36.620
Is there another route?

00:11:38.540 --> 00:11:42.200
Going around Death Valley is the safest option,

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:46.700
but it would be over 600 kilometers
to the supply point.

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:51.040
Death Valley has too many rocks and
crevices to safely drive by moonlight.

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:52.830
"Appare"
Death Valley has too many rocks and
crevices to safely drive by moonlight.

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:58.950
"Appare"
We'll stop at the Valley of Despair
and wait till dawn to enter Death Valley.

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:01.500
I'm sure most everyone will.

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:03.450
The Valley of Despair?

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:08.830
It's a canyon leading to Death Valley
that puts you between the cliffs.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:10.450
Give us beer!

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:13.250
Hurry it up! You're making Gil wait!

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:16.660
You want us to come and drink here instead?

00:12:22.870 --> 00:12:24.040
I'm out.

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:26.330
I'm coming with you.

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:34.790
Appare, go back without me.

00:12:36.410 --> 00:12:39.950
I've got something I have to do.

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:43.370
All right. But we're leaving at midnight.

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:47.200
I know. I'll be back by then.

00:12:57.910 --> 00:12:59.410
Allow me.

00:13:01.370 --> 00:13:05.330
The priority targets are Dylan and TJ.

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:11.330
If they're gone, the rest will be easy.

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:17.660
We'll block the entrance to the
Valley of Despair to slow everyone down.

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:21.830
Once we catch up, we'll plow
right through the barricade

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:24.250
and enter the canyon first.

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:30.700
After that, we'll blast the narrowest part
with dynamite so they can't get through.

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:34.330
Even better, let's crush the lot of 'em
by blasting the rocks--

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:39.160
Idiot! If the race gets canceled,
the prize money's kaput.

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:42.290
We'll just obstruct it a little.

00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:44.950
Ain't that right, Gil?

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:49.700
Though, if one or two people
get squashed, shit happens!

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:54.750
The hell you doing, brat?!

00:13:56.660 --> 00:14:00.410
Were you listening to us just now?

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:09.830
Whew, I'm stuffed!

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:15.290
Hey, Hototo! Pack this in the car!
We'll have something to snack on!

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:18.580
Huh? Hototo? Where's he at?

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:22.040
He left. There was something he had to do.

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:25.410
Huh? Something he had to do?

00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:27.540
Spying ain't good.

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:33.660
I'm not! I'm looking for a guy with
a tattoo on his neck! He killed my dad!

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:35.950
Like I care about your dad.

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:40.620
Murderer! Untie me! Untie me!

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:46.040
Whoa, Gil. Leave this to us.

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:49.540
Hey. Stuff the boy in one of the boxes.

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:53.870
Come tomorrow, he'll go boom!

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:59.580
He's late and it's the dead of night...

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:01.830
Why didn't you ask him anything?

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:08.160
And what then? He has things
he needs to do, but the same goes for me.

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:11.750
Lending an ear is what comrades do!

00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:14.700
He's still just a child.

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:16.450
I'll look for him.

00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:22.750
Hototo! Hototo!

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:24.910
Hototo!

00:15:26.330 --> 00:15:27.620
Hello.

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:30.290
Oh, uh, Richard...

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:33.950
Have you seen Hototo, the little kid with us?

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:35.950
Did something happen?

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:37.540
Actually...

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:41.830
I see. He wants revenge...

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:46.580
Yeah. It was some guy with
a snake tattoo on his neck.

00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:48.290
Gil the Snake.

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:49.250
Huh?

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:52.290
I'm just a small-time bounty hunter.

00:15:52.290 --> 00:15:56.200
Gil and his henchmen
are camping outside the city.

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:59.500
I think he might have gone there.

00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:03.620
Chase, we're ready to set up the trap!

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:07.120
Good. Take the crew and get moving.

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:10.120
Gil and I will leave as soon as it's time for--

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:12.080
Uh, hello?!

00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:13.950
--Huh?
--Who the hell are you?

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:19.910
S-Sorry to bother you! I'm looking for
a little guy named Hototo.

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:22.160
Never heard of the brat.

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:26.580
And unless you get lost, Gil's gonna get mad.

00:16:33.370 --> 00:16:35.200
What's inside that box?!

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:36.330
Huh?

00:16:36.330 --> 00:16:38.000
May I check?

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:39.700
Go and open it.

00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:45.040
But, if there's nothing inside,
you're gonna pay the price.

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:49.290
Um, well... I know I heard something...

00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:59.000
Pardon me... Such a nice box...

00:17:04.700 --> 00:17:06.080
--Hoto--
--Squeak!

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:07.160
...to?

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:08.500
Squeak?

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:09.620
Huh?

00:17:11.450 --> 00:17:13.950
Now then. Time to pay the price.

00:17:13.950 --> 00:17:15.500
--Hototo!
--Huh?

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:17.540
I finally found you!

00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:20.540
--Don't run around all on your own!
--Squeak!

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:23.910
Let's head back, Hototo! Smooch!

00:17:23.910 --> 00:17:28.910
Well, thanks for everything!
Silly Hototo! Smooch!

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:47.290
Just 30 minutes until the leaders leave!
The starting line is coming alive!

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:51.910
What do we do if Hototo doesn't come back?

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:53.700
We leave him behind.

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:55.250
What?!

00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:57.370
Appare...

00:17:57.370 --> 00:18:00.830
You wanna sit and wait till he comes?

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:04.540
It might mean giving up on the race.

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:08.620
He's following his own heart
and I'm following mine.

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:09.910
That's...

00:18:09.910 --> 00:18:14.540
It's fine if you wanna stay behind.
I'll go on alone.

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:21.580
This spot good?

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:23.200
Yeah.

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:30.620
Got it!

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:44.250
The racers will leave based on
their previous finish time!

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:46.250
Next is TJ!

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:55.790
You'll really leave without him?

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:57.040
Stop asking.

00:18:57.040 --> 00:18:59.000
But...!

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:02.080
Xialian! Followed by Richard!

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:04.410
They vanish into the night!

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:19.790
Shit! We're already up next?

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:30.830
Starting next is car number 0, Appare!

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:33.330
Hototo!

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:38.660
Shit! Suit yourself!

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:45.950
Uh-oh! It seems Appare couldn't start!

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:47.290
--Their engine stopped! What's the trouble?!

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:49.330
--Appare?
--Their engine stopped! What's the trouble?!

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:53.870
Most cars won't enter Death Valley
until dawn anyway.

00:19:53.870 --> 00:19:56.410
They'll drive slow at night, too.

00:19:56.410 --> 00:20:00.870
Even if I keep working,
we'll catch up at the Valley of Despair.

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:06.750
If Hototo's not coming, we can
drop his rations for better mileage.

00:20:06.750 --> 00:20:09.790
Appare, you're...

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:15.580
Wha--? Shit! Pick it up, Kosame!

00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:18.160
Here!

00:20:20.250 --> 00:20:26.370
Besides, I'm really close.
A little more and this baby's reborn.

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:28.750
I'll go look again!

00:20:39.660 --> 00:20:41.620
This is...

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:53.620
Huh?

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:58.700
Hototo! Hototo!

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:02.700
Huh?

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:07.910
Hototo?

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:11.540
Hototo...! Hototo!

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:23.620
Appare!

00:21:26.250 --> 00:21:27.700
They came!

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:33.120
Squeak!

00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:34.540
Huh? What the?!

00:21:34.540 --> 00:21:36.000
It's the new Hototo.

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:36.870
Huh?

00:21:36.870 --> 00:21:38.830
--Hototo!
--Right!

00:21:43.330 --> 00:21:46.790
Yeah! Go! Go! Go!

00:21:46.790 --> 00:21:49.330
Here we go!

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:55.540
Where were you?! I was worried sick!

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:57.250
Sorry.

00:21:57.250 --> 00:21:59.660
More importantly, there's bad news!

00:22:03.080 --> 00:22:04.620
With dynamite?!

00:22:04.620 --> 00:22:05.500
Yeah.

00:22:05.500 --> 00:22:10.040
He might hurt Xialian and Al
and block the way to Death Valley!

00:22:10.040 --> 00:22:11.080
Not happening.

00:22:11.080 --> 00:22:12.660
But we'll never catch up to--

00:22:12.660 --> 00:22:14.830
Didn't I tell you?

00:22:14.830 --> 00:22:17.160
This baby's reborn.

00:23:46.700 --> 00:23:47.450
"Next time"

00:23:47.450 --> 00:23:49.910
"Episode 7: FAKE"
